{# ═══ PASSED-ON-TONIGHT SHELF — ANTICIPATION §6.9 R5 per-name "why not" receipts.

   THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. The board above shows the names that BECAME plans. On the
   2026-08-09 artifact the same intake looked at 79 buy-lane names and put down 25 of
   them, and the surface said NOTHING about any of them — so a reader who followed a
   name last week and does not see it tonight could not tell whether it was rejected,
   forgotten, or never looked at. This shelf is the answer, in the reader's words.

   THE STANCE IS "WATCH", NOT "CHASE". Every line here is written so the honest action
   is inaction: the lede says watch and don't chase, and each group names ONE thing the
   name is waiting on. Verdict-style language about a name being thrown out is never
   front-facing (operator ruling 2026-07-27) and no internal token — a status slug, a
   tier name, a gate name — appears in any string this partial can emit. The copy is
   not composed here at all:
   it comes verbatim from `pvr_copy` below, which mirrors engine.prophet_bridge's
   REFUSAL_COPY, and tests/test_prophet_whynot_receipts.py pins the two equal so the
   dashboard shelf and the published receipts can never word the same refusal
   differently.

   TIER DISCIPLINE (doctrine). Glance tier = the group line + the count. A name fails
   MORE THAN ONE gate 14 times out of 25 on the live board, and the headline is only the
   most actionable of them — so the FULL blocker set rides each chip's Tier-2 hover
   (data-tip-en / data-tip-zh). Nothing is hidden, and nothing technical is promoted.
   NO `title=` attribute anywhere: translated text in `title=` is CI-guarded here.

   CONTRACT — ONE argument, `cx`, exactly as engine.prophet_bridge.refusal_receipts
   returns it:
     considered  int   buy-lane rows the intake looked at
     planned     int   considered − passed
     passed      int   names passed on tonight (the rows below)
     unmapped    int   rows whose headline is the fail-closed generic line
     groups      [{reason, en, zh, near, n, names:[{ticker, name, score, why:[code…]}]}]
   Groups arrive pre-ordered and pre-sorted; this partial NEVER re-orders, re-groups or
   re-counts them — `g.n` is the TRUE member count while `g.names` may be capped, which
   is how an overflowing group discloses itself instead of quietly shrinking.

   DEGRADES SILENTLY. No `cx`, or a `cx` with no groups, renders the empty string: the
   panel above must look exactly as it does today on a night when nothing was passed on
   (and on every non-US board, which does not pass this context at all). #}
{% macro t(en, zh='') -%}<span class="l-en">{{ en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ zh if zh else en }}</span>{%- endmacro %}

{# Reason code → (EN, ZH). MIRROR of engine.prophet_bridge.REFUSAL_COPY — the engine is
   the source of truth and the test pins these byte-equal. It is duplicated here (rather
   than threaded through the view-model) because a chip's hover must be able to word EVERY
   code in a row's `why` list, including codes that head no group tonight, and the
   receipts contract ships codes rather than pre-worded strings. Add a code in ONE place
   and the test fails until it is added in the other. #}
{% set pvr_copy = {
  'plan_not_built': ["Cleared every check — no entry plan came together tonight", '各项检查都通过 — 但今晚没能形成完整计划'],
  'already_open':   ['Already has a plan running', '已有在跑的计划'],
  'base_after_event': ["Passed the board's checks — its base re-formed after the signal fired", '通过了榜单检查 — 但基底在信号触发后重新形成'],
  'validation_failed': ["Passed the board's checks — tonight's plan data didn't verify", '通过了榜单检查 — 但今晚的计划数据未能核验'],
  'not_ready':      ["Setting up, but the entry hasn't come", '形态在走，入场点还没到'],
  'ran_too_far':    ['Ran too far — waiting for a pullback', '涨得太急 — 等回调'],
  'stood_down':     ['Standing aside for now', '暂时回避'],
  'grade_low':      ['Signal too weak to act on', '信号强度不足以行动'],
  'conviction_low': ['No setup yet', '暂无买点'],
  'pointing_down':  ['Still heading down', '方向仍朝下'],
  'no_trigger':     ['No entry trigger yet', '还没有入场触发'],
  'unknown':        ['Held back for another reason', '另有原因，暂未纳入']
} %}

{% macro pvr_css() %}
<style>
{# Quiet by construction: the shelf is a closed <details> under a hairline, so it costs
   the board one 12.5px line until the reader asks for it. The only accents are the
   group rails — muted for the general cohort, --pv-wait for the NEAR cohort (the names
   with one identifiable thing between them and a plan), which is the same WAIT hue the
   cards above use for "not yet". Motion is the caret rotation and one hover colour,
   both ≤.16s, so no reduced-motion kill block is owed. #}
.pvr{margin:16px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:10px}
.pvr-sum{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;padding:4px 0;color:var(--text);border-radius:6px}
.pvr-sum::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.pvr-sum:hover .pvr-hd{color:var(--pv-wait)}
.pvr-sum:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--pv-wait);outline-offset:3px}
.pvr-hd{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;transition:color .12s}
.pvr-stat{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.pvr-caret{margin-left:auto;width:7px;height:7px;flex:none;border-right:1.5px solid var(--muted);border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--muted);transform:rotate(45deg) translate(-2px,-2px);transition:transform .16s}
.pvr[open] .pvr-caret{transform:rotate(225deg) translate(-2px,-2px)}
.pvr-lede{margin:9px 0 13px;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted);max-width:62ch}
.pvr-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:13px}
.pvr-g{position:relative;padding:3px 0 3px 12px}
.pvr-g::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:2px;bottom:2px;width:2px;border-radius:2px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 52%,transparent)}
.pvr-g.is-near::before{background:var(--pv-wait)}
.pvr-gh{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px}
.pvr-why{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);line-height:1.35}
.pvr-n{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;margin-left:auto;flex:none;opacity:.75}
.pvr-tks{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px;margin-top:6px}
.pvr-tk{font:600 10.5px/1.65 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:0 5px;min-width:34px;text-align:center;border-radius:4px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 12%,transparent);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 26%,transparent);color:var(--muted)}
.pvr-g.is-near .pvr-tk{color:var(--text);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-wait) 40%,transparent)}
{# The open-plan line sits between the groups and the footnote, quieter than a group
   heading and louder than the stamp — it is accounting, not an instruction. #}
.pvr-open{margin:14px 0 0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted);max-width:62ch}
.pvr-ft{margin:9px 0 0;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);opacity:.8}
{# The era clause is the one hoverable thing in the footnote, so it says so quietly: a
   dotted underline is the house's "there is a receipt here" tell, and `cursor:help` is
   already global on [data-tip-en] (theme.css). No colour — the footnote must stay the
   quietest line on the shelf.

   `.pvr-recon` (the reconstructed-cohort clause) takes the SAME tell, deliberately: it
   is the same kind of thing — provenance at a glance, receipt on hover — and a second
   visual language for it would imply a second kind of importance it does not have. Its
   underline is gated on `[data-tip-en]` because that clause's hover is fail-soft: a
   plan whose date will not parse ships the count with NO receipt, and a dotted tell
   over nothing to hover is a promise the line cannot keep. #}
.pvr-era,.pvr-recon[data-tip-en]{border-bottom:1px dotted color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 55%,transparent)}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvr-g::before{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 70%,transparent)}
{# SPECIFICITY, not decoration — this line is load-bearing. `html[data-theme="light"]
   .pvr-g::before` scores (0,2,2) and OUTRANKS `.pvr-g.is-near::before` at (0,2,1), so
   without an explicit light twin the near rail silently renders muted-grey in light mode
   and the shelf loses its only piece of visual hierarchy. Verified by computed style:
   before this rule every rail returned the same rgb in light. Doctrine §5.8 — light is a
   design target, not a token swap. #}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvr-g.is-near::before{background:var(--pv-wait)}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvr-tk{background:#fff;border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 38%,transparent);color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--text) 70%,var(--muted))}
html[data-theme="light"] .pvr-g.is-near .pvr-tk{color:var(--text)}
@media (max-width:640px){.pvr-why{font-size:12px}}
{# ═ R7 WAVE A (R7-24) — see-all refusal receipts (pvr_receipts) + the Today count
   (pvr_today_count). Neutral surfaces only (Chairman rule 2026-10-18): hairline
   dividers, even borders, ink via --text/--muted/--ink-* — no container edge accent,
   no box-shadow. The summary focus ring is the only accent, and it is an outline. #}
.pvr-rcs{margin:0}
.pvr-rc-hd{margin:0 0 2px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-rc,.pvr-rc-more{border-top:1px solid var(--line-quiet, var(--line))}
.pvr-rc-sum{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;padding:9px 0;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-rc-sum::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.pvr-rc-sum:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink-link);outline-offset:2px}
.pvr-rc-tk{font:600 10.5px/1.65 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.03em;color:var(--muted)}
.pvr-rc-nm{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-rc-sec{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}
.pvr-rc-why{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-left:auto;text-align:right}
.pvr-rc-mh{font-size:12px;font-weight:650;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-rc-bd{display:grid;gap:8px;padding:0 0 11px}
.pvr-rc-row{margin:0;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-rc-k{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}
.pvr-rc-p{margin:0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted);max-width:62ch}
.pvr-rc-a{font-size:11.5px}
.pvr-rc-cap{margin:0 0 2px;font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted)}
.pvr-tc{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0}
.pvr-tc-hd{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text)}
.pvr-tc-n{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.pvr-tc-a{font-size:11.5px}
@media (max-width:640px){.pvr-rc-why{margin-left:0;text-align:left;flex-basis:100%}}
</style>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro pvr_shelf(cx) %}
{%- if cx and cx.groups %}
<details class="pvr">
  <summary class="pvr-sum">
    <span class="pvr-hd">{{ t('Passed on tonight', '今晚未纳入') }}</span>
    {#- The stat is the shelf's whole claim in four characters: of everything looked at,
       this many were DECLINED. `declined`, never `passed` — `passed` includes the rows
       that cleared every gate and already hold a live plan, and headlining those as
       passed-on states something false (see the arithmetic note in
       engine.prophet_bridge.refusal_receipts). Both figures come from the receipts dict —
       never re-derived from `groups|length`, which would silently disagree with the
       engine whenever a group is capped. The groups drawn below sum to exactly this
       number, so a reader who adds them up gets the headline back. #}
    <span class="pvr-stat"><span class="l-en">{{ cx.declined }} of {{ cx.considered }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ cx.declined }} / {{ cx.considered }} 只</span></span>
    <span class="pvr-caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>
  <p class="pvr-lede">{{ t("Watch — don't chase. Each rejoins the board when its setup completes.", '观望，不要追。形态走完，它们会自己回到榜上。') }}</p>
  <ul class="pvr-list">
    {#- `already_open` is deliberately NOT a group here. Those rows cleared every gate and
        are being acted on right now — the reader finds them as CARDS above, so listing 48
        tickers under a "why not" heading would spend the shelf's largest block, its lead
        position and its attention rail on the one cohort that needs no explanation. It
        gets one calm line below the groups instead (doctrine's demotion rule). The engine
        still returns it, so the published receipts stay lossless. #}
    {%- for g in cx.groups if g.reason != 'already_open' %}
    <li class="pvr-g{{ ' is-near' if g.near else '' }}">
      <div class="pvr-gh"><span class="pvr-why">{{ t(g.en, g.zh) }}</span><span class="pvr-n">{{ g.n }}</span></div>
      <div class="pvr-tks">
        {%- for nm in g.names %}
        {#- FULL blocker disclosure, Tier 2. The headline above is only the most
            actionable of this row's reasons; the hover lists every one of them in the
            same specificity order, so the reader can always get from the group line to
            the whole picture. A code with no copy entry falls back to the generic line
            rather than printing a raw slug — same fail-closed rule the engine applies. #}
        {%- set _rs_en = [] %}{% set _rs_zh = [] %}
        {%- for _c in (nm.why or ['unknown']) %}
          {%- set _cp = pvr_copy.get(_c) or pvr_copy['unknown'] %}
          {%- set _ = _rs_en.append(_cp[0]) %}{% set _ = _rs_zh.append(_cp[1]) %}
        {%- endfor %}
        <span class="pvr-tk" data-tip-en="{{ nm.name }} — what's holding it back tonight: {{ _rs_en|join('; ') }}." data-tip-zh="{{ nm.name }} — 今晚未纳入的原因：{{ _rs_zh|join('；') }}。">{{ nm.ticker }}</span>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {#- The open-plan cohort, in one line and no chips. It answers the same question the
      groups above answer — "why isn't this name a new plan tonight?" — but its answer is
      "it already is one, look up", so it needs a count and a direction, not a ticker
      wall. Rendered only when there are any: build_prophet's call site has this cohort,
      build_site's has it whenever last night's plans are still open, and a first-ever run
      has none. #}
  {%- if cx.open_now %}
  <p class="pvr-open">
    <span class="l-en">{{ cx.open_now }} more already have a plan running — they're on the board above.</span>
    <span class="l-zh">另有 {{ cx.open_now }} 只已有在跑的计划 — 就在上方榜单里。</span>
  </p>
  {%- endif %}
  {# ONE footnote, merged (doctrine Law 4): the shelf is a nightly re-draw, not a
     standing verdict — a name here tonight is expected to move, and that is the point of
     the lede. The ERA rides the same line rather than earning a second stamp.

     ERA TIERING (doctrine Law 2 + Law 5). `cx.era` is the chartered literal
     `anticipation-v1-2026-08-08` — a machine identifier, which is exactly the thing Law 2
     bars from the glance tier. So Tier 1 gets the honest PLAIN-WORD form ("same selection
     rules since 8 Aug 2026", read off the literal by engine._refusal_era) and the literal
     itself rides the Tier-2 hover, which is the doctrine's own sanctioned home for a
     provenance receipt. Fail-soft: an era string that stops parsing yields an empty
     `era_since_*` and the clause simply drops — never a wrong date. #}
  <p class="pvr-ft">
    {{- t('Re-drawn nightly', '每晚重绘') -}}
    {%- if cx.era %}
    <span class="pvr-era" data-tip-en="Selection rules in force: {{ cx.era }}. This shelf reports the rules, it never changes them." data-tip-zh="当前选股规则：{{ cx.era }}。本栏只呈现筛选结果，不参与筛选。">
      {%- if cx.era_since_en -%}
      <span class="l-en"> · same selection rules since {{ cx.era_since_en }}</span><span class="l-zh"> · 选股规则自 {{ cx.era_since_zh }} 起未变</span>
      {%- else -%}
      {{ t(' · selection rules unchanged', ' · 选股规则未变') }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {#- RECONSTRUCTED COHORT (§0.10). Rides the SAME merged footnote as the era rather
        than earning a second stamp — Law 4 allows this panel exactly one footnote, and
        this clause is the same KIND of thing the era clause is: provenance for the plan
        population, in plain words at a glance with the detail one hover away.

        It sits LAST on purpose. A reader scanning the shelf wants the shelf; this is
        accounting about the plans on the board above, which is why it is the quietest
        clause on the quietest line.

        WORDING (§0.10, doctrine Law 2). Every string here comes worded from
        engine.prophet_bridge — the template composes nothing, so the count the board
        shows and the note the artifact publishes cannot say different things. The
        internal name of the event ("backfill", the mode slug, the era literal) appears
        NOWHERE, in either tier: the hover is a receipt in plain words, not a decoder.
        No `title=` — translated text in `title=` is CI-guarded here.

        ABSENT, NOT ZERO. `cx.reconstructed` is omitted by the engine whenever nothing
        was reconstructed, so this whole block renders the empty string on every board
        that exists today and the footnote is byte-identical to before. #}
    {%- if cx.reconstructed %}
    {%- set _rc = cx.reconstructed %}
    {#- THE SEPARATOR SITS OUTSIDE THE SPAN, unlike the era clause above. Rendered
        side by side the two underlines ran together through the " · " and read as ONE
        long receipt spanning both clauses — so the dotted rule now starts at this
        clause's first word and there is a clean unmarked gap between the two hovers.
        Verified in the light and dark shots. #}
    {{- ' · ' -}}
    <span class="pvr-recon"
      {%- if _rc.tip_en %} data-tip-en="{{ _rc.tip_en }}" data-tip-zh="{{ _rc.tip_zh }}"{% endif %}>
      {#- No whitespace inside the span: a leading space would be underlined too and put
          the gap back. #}
      <span class="l-en">{{ _rc.en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _rc.zh }}</span>
    </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
</details>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# ═══ R7 WAVE A SLICE A3 — SEE-ALL REFUSAL RECEIPTS + TODAY COUNT (R7-24, R7-05).

   pvr_receipts is the SEE-ALL LANDING list: one disclosure per passed-on name, each
   readable as "not a rejection and not a Wait". pvr_today_count is the Today-side
   count plus ONE plain link to that landing (seat ruling OQ4: plain text link — no
   chevron, arrow or icon; seat ruling OQ5: the refusal title is main's pair, always
   read from pvr_copy['validation_failed'], never retyped here).

   DISPLAY ORDER here is R7-24's, and R7-24's alone: the plan-data refusals
   (validation_failed) lead, then every other name by score descending. That is a
   DIFFERENT contract from pvr_shelf above, which keeps its own never-re-order,
   never-re-group, never-re-count rule over the engine's pre-ordered groups — nothing
   in this macro may change the shelf's grouping, counts or output.

   DEVIATION from the R7 spec's `<button aria-expanded>` wording, ruled by the packet:
   the disclosure is a native <details class="pvr-rc"> + <summary> — the same
   accessible expanded state, without JS.

   PRODUCER GAPs this partial does not paper over: the receipts contract carries no
   per-name `sector` (rendered only when a string one arrives) and no per-check
   "What passed" rows (that heading is omitted, never rendered empty); when capped
   groups ship fewer names than cx.passed, the header keeps the engine's lossless
   total and no copy is invented to explain the difference. #}
{% macro pvr_receipts(cx, limit=4, next_build_en=none, next_build_zh=none, sample=false) -%}
{%- if cx is mapping %}
{#- LOCAL display list only: cx is never mutated and never re-counted — N stays
    cx.passed, the engine's lossless total, even when capped groups ship fewer rows. -#}
{%- set _vf = [] %}{% set _rest = [] %}
{%- for g in (cx.groups or []) %}
  {%- for nm in (g.names or []) %}
    {%- if g.reason == 'validation_failed' %}
      {%- set _ = _vf.append({'nm': nm, 'reason': 'validation_failed'}) %}
    {%- else %}
      {%- set _ = _rest.append({'nm': nm, 'reason': g.reason}) %}
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{#- R7-24's "then the rest by original priority": score descending, STABLE — a
    non-numeric score sorts last in its original order instead of raising. -#}
{%- set _num = [] %}{% set _tail = [] %}
{%- for it in _rest %}
  {%- if it.nm.score is number %}{% set _ = _num.append(it) %}
  {%- else %}{% set _ = _tail.append(it) %}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set _ordered = _vf + (_num|sort(attribute='nm.score', reverse=true)) + _tail %}
{%- set _n_more = (_ordered|length) - limit if (_ordered|length) > limit else 0 %}
{%- if next_build_en is string %}{% set _en_tail = '; the next build is ' ~ next_build_en ~ '.' %}{% else %}{% set _en_tail = '.' %}{% endif %}
{%- if next_build_zh is string %}{% set _zh_tail = '；下次构建在 ' ~ next_build_zh ~ '。' %}{% else %}{% set _zh_tail = '。' %}{% endif %}
{%- if _ordered -%}
<div class="pvr-rcs">
  <p class="pvr-rc-hd">{{ t(cx.passed ~ ' names', cx.passed ~ ' 只') }}</p>
  {%- for it in _ordered %}
  {%- if _n_more and loop.index0 == limit %}
  {#- ONE nested disclosure carries the overflow; the "Showing…" line sits above the
      list it explains. M counts names ACTUALLY present, never cx.passed − limit. -#}
  <details class="pvr-rc-more">
    <summary class="pvr-rc-sum"><span class="pvr-rc-mh">{{ t('Show ' ~ _n_more ~ ' more', '再显示 ' ~ _n_more ~ ' 只') }}</span></summary>
    <p class="pvr-rc-cap">{{ t('Showing ' ~ limit ~ ' of ' ~ cx.passed ~ '. Plan data refusals are listed first, then the rest by original priority.', '显示 ' ~ cx.passed ~ ' 只中的 ' ~ limit ~ ' 只。计划数据未核实的排在最前，其余按建立时优先级排序。') }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- set _cp = pvr_copy.get(it.reason) or pvr_copy['unknown'] %}
  <details class="pvr-rc">
    <summary class="pvr-rc-sum">
      <span class="pvr-rc-tk">{{ it.nm.ticker }}</span>
      <span class="pvr-rc-nm">{{ it.nm.name }}</span>
      {%- if it.nm.sector is string %}<span class="pvr-rc-sec">{{ it.nm.sector }}</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="pvr-rc-why">{{ t(_cp[0], _cp[1]) }}</span>
    </summary>
    {%- if it.reason == 'validation_failed' %}
    <div class="pvr-rc-bd">
      <p class="pvr-rc-row"><span class="pvr-rc-k">{{ t('What didn’t verify', '未能核实的内容') }}</span> — {{ t('Tonight’s plan data', '今晚的计划数据') }}</p>
      <p class="pvr-rc-p">{{ t("Because the plan data didn't verify, we show no entry zone, timing or exit for " ~ it.nm.ticker ~ ' tonight.', '由于计划数据未能核实，今晚不显示 ' ~ it.nm.ticker ~ ' 的入场区间、时机或退出。') }}</p>
      <p class="pvr-rc-p">{{ t('This is not a rejection of the setup and not a Wait. It rejoins the board when its plan data verifies' ~ _en_tail, '这不是否定该形态，也不是等待。计划数据核实后它会重新回到榜单' ~ _zh_tail) }}</p>
      {#- "What passed" needs per-check rows the receipts contract does not carry; an
          empty heading would be a promise with nothing behind it, so it is omitted. -#}
      <a class="pvr-rc-a" href="stock.html#{{ it.nm.ticker }}">{{ t('Open research', '查看研究') }}</a>
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    {#- Any other reason: no invented body copy — just the research link. -#}
    <div class="pvr-rc-bd"><a class="pvr-rc-a" href="stock.html#{{ it.nm.ticker }}">{{ t('Open research', '查看研究') }}</a></div>
    {%- endif %}
  </details>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if _n_more %}</details>{% endif %}
  {%- if sample %}<p class="pvr-ft">{{ t('Sample names and prices for design review, not live signals.', '示例名称与价格，仅供设计评审，并非实时信号。') }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro pvr_today_count(cx, href, sample=false) -%}
{#- The Today-side summary: label, count, ONE plain link (OQ4). Empty for a non-cx,
    a missing key, or anything that is not a positive int — True is not a count. -#}
{%- if cx is mapping and cx.passed is integer and cx.passed > 0 %}
<div class="pvr-tc">
  <span class="pvr-tc-hd">{{ t('Passed on tonight', '今晚未纳入') }}</span>
  <span class="pvr-tc-n">{{ cx.passed }}</span>
  <a class="pvr-tc-a" href="{{ href }}">{{ t('See all ' ~ cx.passed ~ ' passed names', '查看全部 ' ~ cx.passed ~ ' 只未纳入标的') }}</a>
  {%- if sample %}<p class="pvr-ft">{{ t('Sample names and prices for design review, not live signals.', '示例名称与价格，仅供设计评审，并非实时信号。') }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
